  "rationale": "BANDIT-071 is medium-risk bootstrap distribution work. It touches dependency manifest and lockfile state by moving the already-present tsx package from devDependencies to runtime dependencies, narrows package contents through an allow-list, changes installed CLI loader resolution, adds a data-minimal update-check command/cache, and seeds templates/defaults only for installed packages. It does not add public publishing, paid registry, hosted update service, automatic self-update, telemetry, package-manager scripts, CI/release workflows, credentials, production data, merge, push, deploy, or Trust Verifier cutover. Focused packed-install/update-channel tests, full npm test, typecheck, Bandit validation, npm audit, Local Qwen review, CodeRabbit timeout replacement evidence, risk classification, and supply-chain gate evidence cover the landing decision.",
